  "scope": {
    "implementedInternalRead": "GET /internal/v1/migration/company-research-parity/{ticker}",
    "behavior": [
      "Spring reads analyst consensus and per-ticker history evidence from the Node-owned persisted source-cache instead of using the legacy company projection as its expectations calculation input",
      "the source-cache bind mount is read-only and Spring performs no analyst collection, history persistence, scheduler, notification, or Telegram side effect",
      "only analyst-consensus-nasdaq-megacap.json and company-analyst-history-{ticker}.json are streamed; ticker validation prevents path traversal",
      "the consensus snapshot is fresh for one hour and usable stale for at most seven days, matching the Node collector contract",
      "AAPL, MSFT, GOOGL, AMZN, NVDA, META, and TSLA receive expectations; other tickers preserve the existing null expectations contract",
      "the domain policy selects the historical point nearest to the exact UTC instant thirty days earlier, excluding the current date, then applies Node-compatible two-decimal upside/revision and three-decimal analyst-score-revision rounding",
      "file paths and Jackson types remain in the outbound adapter while application and domain receive only framework-free evidence",
      "the response exposes expectationsMatched and legacy/Spring estimate upside, estimate revision, and analyst-score revision before comparing fundamentals, Company Score, and Buy Score",
      "missing, malformed, expired, or unreadable required evidence fails closed with a safe HTTP 502 without exposing an internal path"
    ],
    "remainingInNode": [
      "analyst consensus collection and company analyst history persistence",
      "Yahoo price history used by bottom and reversal signals",
      "SEC submissions, filings, IR, segment, and company enrichment",
      "public company detail calculation and route-cache ownership",
      "company research schedulers and Telegram notifications"
